  "summary_en": "Working paper analysing legal and regulatory challenges of cloud robotics, where physical robots depend on cloud services. It finds the EU framework fragmented, argues for balancing private standard-setting with public law, and examines multi-party liability and data protection issues (controllers/processors, transparency, portability).",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Regulation of cloud robotics is a fragmented patchwork of product safety, machinery, medical device, toy, radio and data protection laws.",
   "Product/service distinction in EU liability rules is strained by cloud robotics' interconnected products.",
   "Balance needed between private standard-setting and public law-making.",
   "Attributing responsibility in multi-party ecosystems is difficult.",
   "Identifying GDPR controllers/processors, ensuring transparency and data portability are unclear in cloud robotics."
